      "file": "syntect/src/parsing/regex.rs",
      "reason": "Reject begin>end before native pointer arithmetic; preserve original safe failure for invalid ranges and UTF-8 end boundary.",
      "previous_sha256": "72d08fe8e0f10fdb6ff10f983b37717be351ec343950884486c9cd167e35b5fb",
      "sha256": "faa84de84ca5f628d23322e0b30fbcced0917ee0c865629e15324fcd03fe4743"
    },
    {
      "file": "onig_sys/Cargo.toml",
      "reason": "Vendor onig_sys so the ended Oniguruma C library is owned in-tree; prohibit publishing the copy and allow the upstream bindings' function-pointer comparisons, which Cargo no longer caps for a path dependency.",
      "previous_sha256": "7915b8ec54838f11c7c66d26dfebe3d106e1ce5d8032690a45a5efe909062b85",
      "sha256": "630663101692bab06c495469b146b830bd8a9ee3bb12fb3edb88afeabcd81152"
    }
  ],
  "ownership": {
    "owner": "Artisan Street",
    "decision_date": "2026-11-18",
    "reason": "Oniguruma upstream ended on 2025-04-24. Syntect's pure-Rust fancy-regex backend passes the parity digests and compiles all 3,732 grammar patterns, but on the parity corpus it took 1.70 s and peaked at 255,724 KB against 0.18 s and 26,516 KB for this bounded Onig backend (release build, 2026-11-18). Capping fancy-regex's delegate DFA size changed neither; capping its NFA size broke grammars. Onig stays, vendored with its C sources so native defects are fixed here.",
    "native_defects": "Patch onig_sys/oniguruma/src in this tree, record the change under followup_changes, rerun verify.py and the validation package, and check the Oniguruma forks in active use for an existing fix first.",
    "revisit": "Switch to regex-fancy when its memory and time on the validation corpus are within reach of these numbers."
  }
}
